      "body": "Most roof problems start small and stay hidden. A lifted shingle here, a tired flashing there, a nail that backed out over ten hot Tri-Cities summers. By the time a stain shows up on your ceiling, the real damage has been happening for a while. A proper inspection catches that early, while it is still a cheap fix. High Point gives you that inspection free, with no obligation and no pressure to sign anything.\n\n## What our roof inspection covers\nTerry gets on the roof himself. He checks the shingles for cracking, curling, and granule loss, the kind of wear our high-desert sun speeds up. He looks hard at the parts that leak first: valleys, flashings around chimneys and vents, and the eaves. He checks the areas you cannot see from the ground, then documents everything with photos so you are looking at your actual roof, not a sales brochure.\n\n## What you get at the end\nYou get a plain-language walk-through and a written report of what he found. If the roof needs work, you get a written estimate, and that estimate is the price you pay. If the roof is fine, we tell you that too. Customers mention this often: Terry does not invent problems to make a job bigger.\n\n## When to book an inspection\nBook one if your roof is more than fifteen years old, if you just rode out a windstorm, if you are buying or selling a Tri-Cities home, or if you have seen anything you cannot explain inside or out. A twenty-minute look now can save you thousands later.\n\n## What a roof inspection costs in the Tri-Cities\nNothing. Our roof inspection and written estimate are free across Kennewick, Pasco, Richland, and the surrounding towns. There is no catch and no obligation to hire us afterward.",
